   219	    printf '    scripts/check-design-refs.sh\n' >&2
   220	    exit 0
   221	  fi
   222	  # The manifest does exactly one git thing: `cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"`.
   223	  # An empty repo satisfies it. `--template=` keeps a user `init.templateDir` (and
   224	  # its sample hooks) out of a directory this script is about to delete.
   225	  git init -q --template= "$SNAPSHOT"
   226	  cd "$SNAPSHOT"
   227	  # MEASURED: git exports `GIT_INDEX_FILE=.git/index` — a RELATIVE path — to
   228	  # hooks, and some versions export GIT_DIR. Any of these left set would make git
   229	  # inside the snapshot resolve against the REAL repository and quietly undo the
   230	  # snapshot.
   231	  unset GIT_DIR GIT_WORK_TREE GIT_INDEX_FILE GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY \
   232	        GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES GIT_COMMON_DIR GIT_PREFIX
   233	fi

codex
The staged snapshot path fails in the repository's normal linked-worktree hook environment because `git init` is run before scrubbing exported Git environment variables. This makes the new pre-commit behavior block relevant commits from worktrees.

Review comment:

- [P1] Scrub Git env before initializing the snapshot — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh3-remainder/scripts/check-design-refs.sh:225-225
  When this pre-commit hook runs from a linked worktree, Git exports `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_INDEX_FILE` as absolute paths to the real worktree admin dir. Because those variables are still set on this `git init`, Git does not create `$SNAPSHOT/.git`; after the later `unset` and `cd "$SNAPSHOT"`, `commission-manifest.sh` cannot `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, so relevant design/state commits are blocked even though the index snapshot was materialized. The env needs to be cleared for the `git init` invocation itself, not only afterward.
